uh hi i'm  chanwe lill i'm an associate professor  at european school of management  technology in berlin and i was educated  in university of cambridge and  since my phd time 10 years ago my  research topic is  always centering around the role of luck  and its  implication for business and society  i probably say everyone may have their  own definition  of luck and to me it's really just that  something unexpected  or random happened to us  but it also bring a very significant  consequence  good or bad if it's good and then we  call it uh we're lucky  and if it's bad and then we're unlucky  the definition of success is the  context-dependent  individual dependent right i teach in  esmt a business school so many people  will define success  like business performances and the  relation  of between success and luck is really a  complicated one  and actually that's the focus of my  research to what extent we can  attribute a success to their  skill interest equality or their effort  or  to being at the right place at the right  time that is luck  for example for business practitioners  my my research question has implication  for them because then  they have to decide to what extent they  should  reward their high performing employees  or to what extent they should imitate  their rivals  best practices  one of the great challenges i think my  research program can contribute  is really try to provide some remedy to  the social inequality we witness  in many different modern societies so  the question is really the social  inequality like the richest people  whether they deserve all the wealth they  obtained  if it's really like based on their  investment insight for example and their  effort of cold land that they serve  but my research findings suggest that  well if you're talking about the richest  a lot of factors beyond their control  matters a lot  and then implies that we should probably  adjust the tax  policy and also redistributed policy  but this is going to be very very  challenging of course so it needs more  and more rigorous evidence to support  these policy changes  so i would say this will be my next  grand challenge based on my research  program  i would like to think some of my  research finding and possible insight  can help  change the world and i think the two  main thing i focus on is the implication  of luck for business and also societies  so on business i really try to design a  policy or design way to help  organizations to promote and reward the  right person  rather than reward some people for their  good luck or bad luck  on the other hand the implication of  love for society is also really  important  because social inequality is huge in  many societies  and many of the the wealthiest people or  the most powerful people  they may not deserve all this attention  they  they got and my research finding can  suggest when  and to what extent this redistributed  policy should be designed  to attenuate the negative consequences  introduced by social inequality
 

